# Desktop

Double-click `OKMate.app` to open the knowledge window (`view`) and restore
`~/.okmate/state` when present. **Choose folder…** uses a native folder
picker, not an HTTP route.

Install the app from [Install](/docs/install/).

## What the window is

The desktop host wraps the same live HTML preview as `okmate view`. It is
not this Rocdown website and not a hosted editor.

## Updates

Sparkle may ask to check automatically after the second launch.
**Check for Updates…** and `brew upgrade --cask okmate` follow GitHub
`releases/latest`. The full autoupdate story is on
[Install](/docs/install/#autoupdate).

A `cargo install` or copied `okmate` on `PATH` does not self-update.

## CLI-only builds

```sh
cargo test -p okmate --no-default-features
```

Those builds omit the webview. `view` without `--no-window` needs the
default `desktop` feature.
